 "processIntrinsic: msg <MessageAST> = (\n				usesIntrinsics:: true.\n				(msg selector = #block: and: [ msg arguments first isKindOfTupleNode ]) ifTrue: [\n						(* A _js block: tuple is a STATEMENT context: each element translates with its own buffer and any hoisted send statements splice in at the element's position. Without this, a send inside e.g. the protected block of a kernel try: would hoist OUT of the try and run unprotected. Argument tuples (call:with: etc.) keep the default behavior -- hoisting to the enclosing buffer correctly evaluates them before the construct. *)\n						^_js block: (processIntrinsicStatements: msg arguments first)\n					].\n				msg selector = #functionOf:body: ifTrue: [\n						(* The body of a _js functionOf: runs WHEN THE GENERATED FUNCTION IS CALLED, not where it is built: it must be a fresh statement context (its hoisted send statements stay inside the function -- without this, sends in an expression-shaped body execute EAGERLY in the enclosing method; AliensForJS expatriateBlock: ran every expatriated callback once at registration time) and a fresh closure level (never the enclosing home's unwrap form). *)\n						| params body buffered |\n						params:: processIntrinsicArg: msg arguments first.\n						closureDepth:: closureDepth + 1.\n						statementBuffers add: List new.\n						body:: processIntrinsicArg: (msg arguments at: 2).\n						closureDepth:: closureDepth - 1.\n						buffered:: statementBuffers removeLast.\n						buffered isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^_js functionOf: params body: body ].\n						^_js functionOf: params\n							body: (_js block: (buffered asArray , {body. }) asArray)\n					].\n				^jsMirror perform: msg selector\n					with: (msg arguments collect: [:arg | processIntrinsicArg: arg ]) asArray\n					ifFail: [:e |\n						('Failed to process an intrinsic during JS translation ' , e printString) out\n					]\n			)",
