 "encodeBytecodeOf: method <IntermediateMethod> = (\n			(* The V5 bytecode record for the MM metadata: a positional array [bytes, literals, numArgs, numLocals, maxStack, bciMap, sourceStart], or null for JS-only methods. bciMap is a flat [bci, start, end, ...] triple list of source ranges whose offsets are relative to the UNIT source the bytecode compiler consumed; sourceStart is the method's own offset in that unit (both compilers parse the same text), so methodRelative = unitRelative - sourceStart + 1 rebases onto the method source stored in MM.source. Literals are emitted in their runtime representation (strings and numbers); a method with a literal that has no such representation (a fraction, an oversized integer) stays JS-only. *)\n\n			| bytecodeMethod literalNodes |\n			bytecodeMethod:: method bytecodeMethod.\n			nil = bytecodeMethod ifTrue: [ ^_js ident: 'null' ].\n			literalNodes:: List new.\n			bytecodeMethod literals do: [:literal |\n					(encodableBytecodeLiteral: literal) ifFalse: [ ^_js ident: 'null' ].\n					literalNodes add: (_js literal: literal)\n				].\n			^_js array: {\n				_js array: (bytecodeMethod bytes collect: [:b | _js literal: b ]).\n				_js array: literalNodes.\n				_js literal: bytecodeMethod argCount.\n				_js literal: bytecodeMethod maxLocals.\n				_js literal: bytecodeMethod maxStack.\n				encodeBciMapOf: bytecodeMethod.\n				_js literal: (nil = method sourceStart ifTrue: [ 0 ] ifFalse: [ method sourceStart ]).\n			}\n		)",
